{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met all responsibility-chain duties without a serious or minor chain error: it repeatedly screened red flags, reconciled gastric and hypertension medications without unsafe self-change, recognized the gastric cancer pathway while avoiding staging/operability overreach, and built a concrete follow-up/urgent-care plan. It completed multiple high-order points, especially correcting misconceptions about pathology/immunohistochemistry/lymph nodes and making the plan feasible around caregiver fatigue and handoff logistics. Closure was bounded and executable, with a pre-admission waiting plan, owners, timing, monitoring, and emergency thresholds. Therefore the deterministic grade is 5 rather than 4.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00547",
        "explanation": "Final plan gives bounded waiting period for the external owner/process.",
        "quote": "等1–3个工作日通常不会因此耽误治疗"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00547",
        "explanation": "Final plan assigns fallback owner and timing if handoff stalls.",
        "quote": "若到第3个工作日仍没通知，主动联系外科或住院处确认"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00547",
        "explanation": "Final plan preserves safety by specifying emergency escalation.",
        "quote": "立即急诊/120"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The episode closes after the patient has an active external pathway: pre-admission/bed call within 1–3 working days, a clear fallback to contact surgery/admissions, home monitoring and medication boundaries, and explicit emergency triggers. Residual staging and treatment-plan uncertainty is acceptable because it is assigned to the inpatient surgical pathway rather than solved online.",
